// A fused variant pattern tests only the TAG, so two arms carrying the
// SAME tag at different arities are indistinguishable to the kernel: the
// first one wins and its payload slots read as 0.
//
//   interp: 7    (`A(i64:7)` matches the arity-1 arm, n = 7)
//   jit:    -1   (the arity-0 arm's tag test passes first)
//
// Fusion verified separately: the CLI form
//     let x: [`A, `A(i64)] = `A(i64:7);
//     let r =
//     #[native]
//     select x { `A => i64:-1, `A(n) => n };
//     println("[r]")
// compiles in JIT mode (so `#[native]` passes — a genuinely fused
// region) and prints 7 / -1. The wrapper form below is the oracle pin.
//
// The union `[`A, `A(i64)]` is legal and typechecks — a variant's
// identity is (tag, arity), and the node-walk's `StructPatternNode`
// checks both (its variant arm is length-guarded and falls to `_ => ()`
// on a mismatch, which is why the interp reaches the second arm). The
// emitter's tag-equality test drops the arity half.
//
// Same shape at other arities — see 01.
//
// Fix: the emitted variant condition must test the payload COUNT as well
// as the tag — the value carries its arity (a variant is a tagged array
// whose length is 1 + arity), and the arm knows the arity it expects, so
// the condition is one extra integer compare against the payload
// length. Every payload READ downstream of that condition is then sound;
// today an arity-0 arm can be taken for an arity-2 value and a
// `variant_payload_read` returns `T::default()` for the missing slots
// (totalized since crash-triage-jul2026, so it is a wrong value rather
// than UB — but it is silently wrong).
//
// Related: select-lit-leaf-union-slot-aug2026 is the same shape of bug
// one level down (a literal leaf over a union-typed slot, fixed by
// requiring the leaf's static type to freeze to the literal's prim
// family). This is the variant-arity twin and wants the same treatment:
// when the kernel cannot distinguish two arms, DE-FUSE rather than
// guess.
{ let x: [`A, `A(i64)] = `A(i64:7); select x { `A => i64:-1, `A(n) => n } }
